Task 2: Deploy and Validate the Role Against Managed Nodes
Subtask 2.1: Write and Run a Role-Based Playbook
Create a playbook that consumes the webserver role with overridden variables:
cd /home/student/ansible-labs
cat > webserver-role-playbook.yml << 'EOF'
---
- name: Deploy Web Server using Custom Role
  hosts: web_servers
  become: yes
  vars:
    webserver_admin_email: "lab-admin@alnafi.com"
    webserver_port: 8080
  roles:
    - webserver

- name: Verify deployment
  hosts: web_servers
  tasks:
    - name: Check if web server is accessible
      uri:
        url: "http://{{ ansible_default_ipv4.address }}:8080"
        method: GET
        return_content: yes
      register: web_response
      delegate_to: localhost

    - name: Display web server response
      debug:
        msg: "Web server is responding with status: {{ web_response.status }}"
EOF
Run the playbook with verbose output:
ansible-playbook -i inventory webserver-role-playbook.yml -v
Expected result: The play recap shows ok and changed tasks for both hosts with failed=0. The final debug task prints Web server is responding with status: 200.

Confirm the deployed page manually and test idempotency:
curl http://10.0.1.10:8080
curl http://10.0.1.11:8080
ansible-playbook -i inventory webserver-role-playbook.yml
Expected result: curl returns the rendered HTML containing the hostname and IP of each node. On the second playbook run, the play recap shows changed=0 for all tasks except the uri verification task, confirming idempotency.

Deliverable: A successful playbook run with failed=0 and confirmed idempotent second run (no unexpected changed tasks).

